Query: Read /workspace/autoresearch/README.md, /workspace/autoresearch/program.md, /workspace/autoresearch/context.md, and /workspace/autoresearch/AGENTS.md first. 
Then read ${SGLANG_REPO}/context.txt and ${SGLANG_REPO}/marconi.txt if they exist.

You are using /workspace/autoresearch only as the evaluation harness and experiment log. The code to improve is in /workspace/sglang on branch marconi-eviction or its 
current clean worktree equivalent. Do not commit.

Environment and operating assumptions for this cron run:
- workspace: /workspace/autoresearch
- target repo: /workspace/sglang
- target branch: marconi-eviction
- hardware proxy: 1xH100
- model: nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-Nano-9B-v2
- tensor parallel size: 1
- eval mode: fast
- context length: 32768
- public API must stay aligned with --radix-eviction-policy marconi
- for this Nemotron setup, use MARCONI_EXTRA_SERVER_ARGS='--mamba-scheduler-strategy no_buffer' when running train.py

At the very start of the cron execution, explicitly rebuild continuity before changing anything:
1. cd /workspace/autoresearch
2. ensure these env vars are set for this run:
   - SGLANG_REPO=/workspace/sglang
   - MARCONI_MODEL_PATH=nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-Nano-9B-v2
   - MARCONI_TP_SIZE=1
   - MARCONI_MIN_GPUS=1
   - MARCONI_EVAL_MODE=fast
   - MARCONI_CONTEXT_LENGTH=32768
   - MARCONI_RESULTS_DIR=/workspace/autoresearch/results
   - MARCONI_EXTRA_SERVER_ARGS=--mamba-scheduler-strategy no_buffer
3. read /workspace/autoresearch/results.tsv
4. read /workspace/autoresearch/baselines.tsv if it exists
5. inspect git branch, commit, and diff state in /workspace/sglang
6. read /workspace/autoresearch/context.md again
7. continue from the best current local repo state you find rather than starting from scratch

This cron execution is bounded. Do exactly 3 research iterations, no more and no less.

For each of the 3 iterations:
1. inspect current target repo branch/commit/dirty state
2. form one narrow Marconi autotune policy-quality hypothesis
3. make one small code-level change in /workspace/sglang only
4. run exactly one experiment from /workspace/autoresearch with:
   uv run --no-sync train.py > run.log 2>&1
5. read the summary from /workspace/autoresearch/run.log
6. append a row to /workspace/autoresearch/results.tsv
7. keep the local target-repo change only if it improves autotune-enabled throughput for this proxy setup; otherwise revert just your last change
8. do not commit

Constraints:
- do not mainly edit the harness unless it is clearly broken
- do not broaden into unrelated Marconi work
- do not change benchmark methodology in a way that breaks comparability
- do not hardcode a hidden favorite eff_weight fallback
- prefer the smallest justified policy change
- keep the public user contract aligned with --radix-eviction-policy marconi
- scheduled run must stay bounded to 3 iterations

Primary objective:
- improve autotune-enabled request throughput
- and, when a main-branch non-Marconi baseline is available in /workspace/autoresearch/baselines.tsv, beat that reference on throughput and TTFT

Secondary objective:
- lower mean TTFT

At the end of this cron execution, produce a concise summary containing exactly:
- iterations completed
- best throughput seen this run
- best mean TTFT seen this run
- whether any local change is worth keeping
- current target branch and commit
- delivery note that results.tsv was updated in /workspace/autoresearch
